  "all_ingredients_flat": "russet potatoes, aquafaba, onion powder, garlic powder, red chilly powder, salt",
  "instructions": "Wash and French fry cut 2 russet potatoes (I used Cuisinart 14-cup Food Processor). Dry them with a paper towel. Add about 2 tsp aquafaba to the cut potatoes and coat thoroughly. Air fry at 400F till crispy. Turn it over when half done. Make a seasoning of equal portions of onion & garlic powder with red chilly powder and salt to taste. Once the fries are done completely (golden & crisp), add seasoning powder and mix thoroughly.",
  "cooking_methods": [
    "air-fry"
  ],
  "serving_suggestion": "Enjoy hot dipped in homemade WFPB ketchup!",
  "notes": "homemade WFPB ketchup",
